te_title:"What it takes to go live",ai_gate_wf:"Holds up across periods: {v} — needs {need} or more",ai_gate_wf_min:"weakest period {v} — needs {need} or more",ai_gate_wf_none:"Check across periods: starts at {need} outcomes, {n} so far",ai_hint:`Cortex is an oracle: a trained model that estimates the chance the price follows the wallets you track. When many independent wallets move the same way, it puts a number on it.

It looks at 47 signals, not just the flow: volumes and wallet counts, returns over an hour, six hours and a day, volatility and its spikes, ATR, RSI, trend, MACD, funding, open interest, liquidations, leverage, liquidity, the Bitcoin regime and market breadth.

Events it reads from its own data: how long ago the coin was listed, how far the volume broke out of its own week, and how hard the price was shaken in the last hours. A listing, a hack or a piece of news arrives as a trace in the numbers — and that trace it can learn from. The news text itself it does not read: there is none in its history, so there is nothing there to learn.

The shape of the move it marks up itself: the series is cut into legs, and their lengths are what gets counted — how deep the pullback is and whether it lands on a Fibonacci level, whether the new leg runs longer than the last, how many legs in a row go the same way. Waves the way an analyst draws them a machine cannot count: two people draw them differently. What it counts is the part of that drawing which is arithmetic.

The model decides for itself: the horizon — six hours or a day, the stop and the targets, and the share of the deposit worth risking.

Until it beats a coin flip on data it has never seen, it is not accepted: the formula works instead, and the model screen says so. This is an estimate, not investment advice.`,ai_hist_avg:"Average move:",ai_hist_btn:"📜 Signal history",ai_hist_empty:"No completed signals yet.",ai_hist_head:"{a} of {b} signals reached the target",ai_hist_hours:"h ago",ai_hist_none:"neither",ai_hist_open:"{n} signals running — first result in {h}",ai_hist_plans:"Plans closed:",ai_hist_rate:"Hit rate:",ai_hist_rest:"the rest hit the stop or went nowhere",ai_hist_sl:"by stop",ai_hist_title:"Signal history",ai_hist_tp:"by target",ai_hits_of:"right {n} times out of 100",ai_hours:"{n}h",ai_like_coin:"no better than a coin flip yet",ai_long:"Long",ai_loss_hint:"next to it, the same error without the model: lower means more accurate",ai_lv_formula:"Levels from volatility",ai_lv_model:"Levels from the model",ai_market:"Market entry",ai_mode_formula:"Formula · model still learning",ai_mode_model:"Model",ai_model_ok:"The model is working",ai_none_now:"No coin passed the filter right now",ai_not_passed:"Model not accepted yet",ai_p_dn:"chance of a fall in {h}",ai_p_short:"chance of a rise",ai_p_short_dn:"chance of a fall",ai_p_up:"chance of a rise in {h}",ai_pass_hint:"one lucky pass proves nothing: we check again on later data",ai_perp:"Perps",ai_plan:"Trade plan",ai_price_now:"price now",ai_rel_few:"few signals — the number does not mean much yet",ai_rel_got:"happened",ai_rel_said:"said",ai_rel_title:"Promised and happened",ai_risk:"risk",ai_sell:"Sell",ai_short:"Short",ai_since_signal:"since the signal",ai_spot:"Spot",ai_src_formula:"Formula",ai_src_model:"Model",ai_src_none:"No model signals yet — it has not passed its checks",ai_src_title:"Who made the signals",ai_st_acc:"Accuracy:",ai_st_base:"baseline",ai_st_btn:"🧠 Model",ai_st_cal:"Calibration:",ai_st_coin:"coin flip",ai_st_gate:"threshold",ai_st_loss:"Estimate error",ai_st_quality:"Model quality",ai_st_ready:"Outcomes ready:",ai_st_sampl